# Project Rules

## Session continuity

Before doing anything, check if `plan.md` and `memory.md` exist in the repo root.
If they do, read them first — they contain the project plan, progress, and architectural
decisions from previous sessions (possibly from a different agent or interface).

Pick up where the last session left off. Do not restart or re-plan work that is already done.

## Working style

- Commit to feature branches, never to `main`.
- Update `plan.md` when you complete tasks.
- Update `memory.md` when you make architectural decisions.
- Keep responses concise — the user may be reading on a phone.
- Ask one question at a time.
- Be direct. No filler.
